199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Based on research and site visits to 12 hospitals, the researchers made several recommendations regarding design. First, windows are needed to provide natural light. According to the Ontario Long-Term Care Design Manual, Bedrooms must have at least one window that provides a direct view to the outdoor. The proper windows expand the view of the natural landscape outside the room and helps increase the amount of light. At the same time, LTC also specifies that windows need to be shaded during certain seasons. One of the hospitals uses bamboo and greenery to create shadows, and large windows are also used to increase natural light. This is a design that helps to communicate between the indoor and outdoor spaces and increases the occupants' connection to nature.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Warm walls, the use of landscape paintings, the placement of ornamental fish, and the use of natural materials in the furniture are all listed in the article as biophilic designs. Ornamental fish serve as direct nature-experiencing element, providing the occupants with the opportunity to interact with living organisms. The rest are non-nature-experiencing elements that enhance their connection to nature and provide them with benefits more psychologically and perceptually.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
201 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The researchers conducted a statistical survey to assess the benefits of using each element. The most important of the conclusions were "creating a relatively inward-looking spatial environment, similar to a cave in nature, with long, open views in the foreground", "using real plants or specimens, green roofs, green walls", and "using natural construction or decorative materials" \(Zhao, Zhan, & Xu, 2022\). From the results of the public's assessment of the importance of biophilic design elements, it can be concluded that they need small spaces that provide shelter and prefer direct natural elements.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
202 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
