/T (Space planning in healthcare environments should prioritize the patient's acoustic experience and privacy needs. Designers need to consider current and future noise sources that may affect the facility. Designs should incorporate noise mitigation strategies such as the use of barriers, acoustic blinds, and the selection of quieter equipment to ensure a rehabilitative environment for patients.)
