321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 954 0 R
/E (Each RHA shall be a clearly defined individual unit, located on the same floor, for a maximum of 32 residents. Resident spaces \(including bedrooms, bathrooms, dining areas, lounge and activity areas\) and staff work areas \(including records areas, treatment spaces, equipment and supply storage and utility spaces\) shall be located within each RHA.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 955 0 R
/E (Each bedroom shall have a maximum of two beds and a minimum of 12.08 square meters \(130 square feet\) of usable net floor space for single bedrooms and a minimum of 10.68 square meters \(115 square feet\) of usable net floor space per resident is required for double bedrooms. Bedrooms must have en-suite bathrooms with a minimum bathroom doorway width of 914 mm \(3 ft.\) and sufficient turnaround space to accommodate a wheelchair or walker.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 956 0 R
/E (Emergency call systems, and locks that are easy for residents and staff to open from the outside near the bed and toilet are required.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 957 0 R
/E (Each RHA must have a workspace for caregivers to do their work. There must be a space on each floor of the RHA that supports the therapy program. At least one therapy room is required for every three RHAs.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 958 0 R
/E (Each RHA must have space to store needed medications, supplies, and equipment that should be easily accessible to caregivers without intruding into residents' personal space.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
