463 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1067 0 R
/E (Firstly, exposure to natural light improves the mental and physical health of patients, and a large number of glass windows have been set up to achieve this. In the center, an openable window is set up, which can be opened at an angle that is not too large, depending on the requirements. A window sill is provided for the patients to use or to place green plants to enhance the patients' contact with nature.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
464 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1068 0 R
/E (To avoid the bathroom obscuring the window area, as well as to provide privacy, it is set in the upper left corner. An angled door avoids the oppressive feeling of the corridor and facilitates patient access. The interior of the bathroom is accessible, and the walk-in shower has a seat and handles in it, which are safety considerations.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
465 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1069 0 R
/E (A closet and adjustable end table are placed at the foot of the bed for easy access to the patient's personal belongings. TVs and cabinets across from the bed provide entertainment and storage space without interfering with the main walkway, and they are positioned so that patients can watch TV from the comfort of their bed.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
466 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1070 0 R
/E (Beds can be reached from both sides for easy access to caregivers. The spacious corridors are also easy to use and access for special populations.)
/Pg 26 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
