476 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1079 0 R
/E (The following healthcare interior design recommendations can be gleaned from research:)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
477 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1080 0 R
/E (Ensure rooms have enough natural light and provide a visual connection between indoors and outdoors through large windows or sunrooms to promote patients' mental and physical well-being. Use natural paintings as well as furniture made of natural materials to enhance the patient's connection with nature and boost psychological feelings. Use appropriate shading during different seasons to ensure that sunlight enters the room, but also to avoid excessive sunlight. At the same time, the use of dynamic and dispersed natural light to mimic the natural environment contributes to the emotional and physical well-being of patients.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
478 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1081 0 R
/E (Provide patients with private resting spaces, such as single or double occupancy rooms, to reduce stress and enhance a sense of security. Ensure rooms have emergency call systems. Consider the patient's acoustic experience and privacy needs in the design and use soundproofing strategies to create a quiet therapeutic environment. Ensure the design is flexible to accommodate different treatment needs and activity types, including multi-functional furniture and adjustable lighting systems.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
479 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1082 0 R
/E (Implement clear navigation systems in healthcare facilities, including clear and simple signage, digital navigation tools and easily recognizable navigational elements to help patients, visitors and staff find target locations more easily.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
480 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1083 0 R
/E (In terms of material selection, choose hygiene-compliant interior surfaces, such as antimicrobial materials, easy-to-clean surfaces, and products that are fire-resistant and low in VOCs to ensure a sanitary and safe healthcare environment.)
/Pg 27 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
